{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/936188-berlin-1945-after-world-war-2","id":936188,"title":"Berlin 1945, after World War 2","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-23T12:27:45-07:00","id":936188,"title":"Berlin 1945, after World War 2","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> I am running a game of Werewolf, set in that time period, and while the Dark Eras focuses on Demons in that time, I was thinking of making Changelings be the main supernaturals in the city. But since I do not know enough about them, I turn to this forum.<br /> <br /> What kind of Courts do you envision in the city?<br /> How would they interact with the other supernaturals? (mainly Vampires, Mages, and Werewolves)<br /> What sample members would you create for such a setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T12:31:23-07:00","id":936189,"title":"","content":"I know this is mainly focused on asking about the Changelings, but remember that WWII was the formal creation of Task Force: Valkyrie, so expect the Allies to have several conspiracies working within the new structure of power keeping a close eye on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T13:42:45-07:00","id":936219,"title":"","content":"In the Demon Dark Era, it mentions in a sidebar that West and East Berlin are ruled by Seasonal Courts, where the Summers have banded together are are not only working on, but succeeding in, &quot;domesticating&quot; the Hedge, creating towers and garrisons to bind it, even as others worry about the eventual pushback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:00:38-07:00","id":938157,"title":"","content":"I'd also look at the Grimm Chapter and Compare and contrast the two eras, both occurring in Germany.<br /> <br /> Here is the interesting thing you'll notice. When the Godmachine is asendant in a region, the Gentry seem to have much less influence and when the Gentry are thriving and active in the mortal world within a region, the Godmachine's influence in that region wanes. The Gentry and the Godmachine are like oil and water.<br /> <br /> So since the Gentry are retreating by 1945, allowing the Hedge to be domesticated, that hints that the Godmachine might be backing the Changelings in their efforts, which puts the Changeling courts in direct opposition to the local demons.<br /> <br /> Your werewolves could be caught in the middle of a fued between them, a neutral third party being pressured by both sides to take a side.<br /> <br /> For an extra level of intrigue you can have Changeling spies from nearby German cities that use none seasonal court systems, who are trying to figure out what Berlins Seasonal Court is up to.<br /> <br /> And maybe the Communist side of Berlin has a Chinese Embassy dominated by Changelings of the Directional Courts, who are also members of the Chinese Communist Party for added intrigue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:59:45-07:00","id":938255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/936188-berlin-1945-after-world-war-2?p=938157#post938157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And maybe the Communist side of Berlin has a Chinese Embassy dominated by Changelings of the Directional Courts, who are also members of the Chinese Communist Party for added intrigue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would doubt it. This is 1945, the city is still under joint military occupation by the Four Powers. Although the Soviets handed over the Western sectors of Berlin in July, the Allies will be jointly running the city administration until at least 1946.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"ht